Clearing a ready thread's share, by a revoke or by the destroy of its pool,
forgets the share before the thread leaves its ring, so the thread stays on it.
The next turn of the share would run a thread that has no share, or memory that is no longer a thread;
a share's ring holds only live threads bound to it.

Caught-by: fuzz fuzz-pmp8 fuzz-grain32 fuzz-work test qemu-replay
Report: queue holds a thread it is not for
Report: thread on no queue is linked into one

